args : --fresco
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

Named flexible parameter annotations execute through a higher-order call
(fun(f){f})(fun(y:%a){y:%a})(42)
args : --fresco
stdout : 42 : Int

Annotated curried parameters use the supplied forall scope
sig f:forall a,b.(a)->(b)->b fun f(x:a)(y:b){y:b} (f(0)(42),f(0)(true))
args : --fresco
stdout : (42, true) : (Int, Bool)

Nested parameter annotations can use a local alias
(fun(){typename Local=Int; fun(x:Local){x}})()(42)
args : --fresco
stdout : 42 : Int

Annotated callback arguments retain their surrounding forall binders
sig use:forall a.((a)->a,a)->a fun use(f,x){f(x)} sig run:forall a.(a)->a fun run(x:a){use(fun(y:a){y:a},x)} (run(42),run(true))
args : --fresco
stdout : (42, true) : (Int, Bool)

